+### Turning Wiki Reads Off
+
+To stop agents from reading the wiki (to seed or inform their context), add this to `.ta/workflow.toml`:
+
+```toml
+[wiki]
+seed_context = false
+```
+
+With it set, the TA MCP gateway refuses `ta_wiki_search`, `ta_wiki_get` and `ta_wiki_types` for every agent, including chat-mode sessions. Each refusal names the setting and the file, and says how to turn reads back on. Writes are unaffected: `ta_wiki_create` and `ta_wiki_update` still queue changes for review in the goal's draft.
+
+The default is `true`; a missing `[wiki]` section or key leaves reads on. A value that is not `true` or `false` is an error that names `.ta/workflow.toml` and `seed_context`. The setting is read on every call, so no restart is needed. While it is `false`, `ta doctor` shows a `wiki.seed_context` line so you can see why reads are refused. To allow reads again, set `seed_context = true` or remove the key.
+
 ### Wiki Writes Are Reviewed
 
 `ta_wiki_create` and `ta_wiki_update` do not write to the wiki when an agent calls them. They check the input and queue the change in the goal's draft. Nothing reaches Wayfinder until you approve and apply that draft. `ta_wiki_search`, `ta_wiki_get` and `ta_wiki_types` are unchanged and read live.
